From fa518cc3d76db0f4daec41352ef2befa36e6c56e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayoub5550 <140963656+ayoub5550@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:22:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] compat: run PS5 native homebrew (DOOM, Hello World) under the
 HLE runtime

Homebrew built on the clean-room libc.prx runtime links differently from
retail titles; each change below was a crash or a wrong result in DOOM
(doomgeneric as a native PS5 app) or the boilerplate's Hello World.

- library-aware LLE redirect: an import goes to a loaded module's export
  only when that module exports the NID under the library the import names
  (DT_SCE_IMPORT_LIB / DT_SCE_EXPORT_LIB); otherwise HLE. The runtime's
  libc.prx exports stub malloc/free that return 0.
  SHARPEMU_IGNORE_IMPORT_LIBRARY=1 restores the old behaviour.
- HLE data symbols __stdinp/__stdoutp/__stderrp/__isthreaded, preferred
  over a library-mismatched module export.
- sceKernelSendNotificationRequest: logs [KERNEL][NOTIFY] <text>.
- the HLE libc heap is reachable from HLE functions (fread/fgets/fwrite,
  memset, PhysicalVirtualMemory) through HostHeapRanges, including host
  pointers above 2^47 on 48-bit arm64 hosts under FEX.
- direct mappings at/above the map search base bump the next virtual
  address; HLE data falls back to host allocation.
- libc HLE: strncasecmp puts putc putchar mkdir system toupper atoi atof
  strdup remove __swbuf; printf integer precision (%.3d).
- VideoOut: SHARPEMU_LOG_FPS=1, SHARPEMU_DUMP_VIDEOOUT_EVERY/_MAX/_DIR,
  detiled dumps of 32bpp tiling-mode-0 buffers.
- SHARPEMU_LOG_RESERVE_EXCEPTIONS=1; host Execute views map R+X.
